# Architecture Patterns

## Server vs client

- Default: Server Components in `app/`
- `"use client"` only for state, effects, event handlers, or browser APIs
- Fetch and secrets stay on the server (Server Components, Route Handlers, or Server Actions)

```tsx
// ✅ app/courses/page.tsx — fetch here, pass props
export default async function CoursesPage() {
	const courses = await listCourses();
	return <CourseList courses={courses} />;
}

// ❌ Do not fetch inside reusable presentational components
```

## Presentational UI (`components/`)

Same idea as `@netmifi/design` in mono:

- Props in, UI out
- No routing, no data fetching, no `process.env`
- Framework-agnostic so the file can move later

```tsx
// ✅ Portable
export function CourseCard({ title, href }: { title: string; href: string }) {
	return <a href={href}>{title}</a>;
}

// ❌ Next-coupled reusable component
"use client";
import { useRouter } from "next/navigation";
export function CourseCard({ id }: { id: string }) {
	const router = useRouter();
	return <button onClick={() => router.push(`/courses/${id}`)}>Open</button>;
}
```

Pass `Link`, callbacks, or `href` from `app/` when you need Next.js navigation.

## Data and env

- Catalogs and demo rows: `mock-data/` (import `@/mock-data/universities`, `@/mock-data/skills`)
- Matching, invites, agreements: `lib/` — not inside components
- Typed env from `lib/env.ts` once it exists

## Figma

Map each frame to a section or card. Do not recreate a whole screen as a single component.

Implement **mobile-first**. Treat the phone composition as the product; desktop is optional and only when specified.
